Description: Lex the spaced Elvis operator "? :" as one token
 Twig registers "? :" as an alias of the Elvis operator "?:", so its lexer
 returns "a ? : b" as name, operator "? :", name. twig-lexer returned "?"
 and ":" as two punctuation tokens. Whitespace between the two characters may
 be any amount, like other operators containing a space.
Author: Numiko
Origin: other, https://github.com/twigphp/Twig/blob/v3.28.0/src/Extension/CoreExtension.php
Forwarded: not-needed
Twig-Reference: 3.17.1
Test: test/fixtures/twig/operators.twig (parity with Twig 3.28.0); test/syntax-coverage.test.ts; npm run test:upstream
Last-Update: 2026-09-24
---
diff --git a/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts b/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts
index ea6ec7c..b206c31 100644
--- a/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts
+++ b/src/main/lib/Lexer.ts
@@ -200,6 +200,7 @@ export class Lexer {
 
         if (this.level === 3) {
             this.operators.push('xor', 'has some', 'has every', '?:', '===', '!==', '?.');
+            this.operators.push('? :');
         }
 
         this.tagPair = ['{%', '%}'];
